=== Flash device in physical memory map ===
BCM6348 SoCs allow only to load a bootloader from the fixed address 0x1FC00000. This restricts the max size of the flash memory to be 4 MB, unless the bootloader makes some trick to allow bigger sizes, like our redboot does:
  * The bootloader is first loaded from the physical address 0x1FC00000 (the middle of the flash where the bootloader really lives), and then the bootloader itself remaps whole flash to see the 8MB. The problem is that once remapped the bottom sectors are seen as if they were in the middle of the flash.\\ {{media:thomson:livebox1_flash_remapping.png?300|}}


